; A parameter list naming a value that is not in the entry block.
;
; Parameters are the function's interface. The verifier's parameter
; section was DEAD CODE on any file read from disk, because the reader
; never rebuilt f.params -- param_count was 0 for every loaded module, so
; every check below it iterated zero times. This fixture is what makes
; that section observable: it only fails if the list is rebuilt AND
; checked.
;
; Here the AIR_PARAM is defined in b2, not the entry block b1.
func f entry=b1
  block b1
    %1 = const.int ival=0  [range=0..0 w=64]
    jump b2
  end
  block b2  ; pred=b1
    %2 = param name=late
    ret %2
  end
endfunc
